LightHA is MIT licensed (see LICENSE). It bundles these third-party files under their own terms:

- app/src/main/res/raw/wake.mp3: the wake sound from Voice Satellite
  (https://github.com/jxlarrea/voice-satellite-card-integration, custom_components/voice_satellite/sounds/wake.mp3),
  unmodified, licensed AGPL-3.0. Its source is that repository.

- app/src/main/assets/wakeword/hey_luna.tflite and .json: the Hey Luna microWakeWord model by Tater Totterson
  (https://github.com/TaterTotterson/Tater-Wake-Words, microWakeWordsV6), MIT licensed
  (Tater-Wake-Words commit ca39092, "Add MIT license").

LightHA does not bundle the rest of the Tater Wake Words catalog. When you pick one in Settings, the tablet downloads
that model straight from the Tater-Wake-Words repository, under that repository's terms.

- app/src/main/cpp: the microWakeWord engine from the Home Assistant Android app, Apache-2.0 (see app/src/main/cpp/NOTICE).

- The Okay Nabu, Hey Jarvis and Hey Mycroft models: see the author fields in app/src/main/assets/wakeword/*.json.
